README.md

text
# User Registration Feature
**Goal:** Handle user sign-up, email verification, and welcome flow  
**Linked Code:** /app/Users/RegisterController.php  
**Status:** Complete ✅  
**Created:** 2025-10-23  

### Routes
- POST /register
- GET /email/verify

### Dependencies
- Queue system (Redis)
- Notification channels (Mail + SMS)

### Success Metric
95% registration success rate without timeouts.
decisions.md

text
# Decision Record: Registration Flow
**Chosen Pattern:** Form Request Validation + Event Listeners  
**Alternatives Considered:** Inline validation, Middleware handling  
**Team Debate Outcome:**  
Form Requests give cleaner controllers and reusable validation rules.

**Consequences:**  
Reduced duplication; improved testability.
✅ Final Deliverable Summary
Every Laravel project includes a /brain directory beside /app and /config.

Each feature has its own folder inside /brain/features.

Architecture decisions are tracked through ADRs in /brain/architecture/ADRs.

All tests, deployments, and security updates are traceable to their corresponding brain entry.

No merge or deployment occurs unless /brain is updated.

This adaptation of the Brain Rule leverages Laravel’s service providers, MVC patterns, folder-by-feature structure, PHPDoc standardization, and ADR methodology.​
The result is a Laravel-specific knowledge architecture, turning each project into a self-documenting, self-explanatory ecosystem ready for any scale of collaboration or future re-entry.